% ============================================================================
% water-share.query.adj — worked recall over the water-share library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to answer "what share of fresh
% water is locked up in ice?" (direct, returning the share AND what it is a
% share of), "what shares are given for surface freshwater?" (reverse by
% BASE — lakes and rivers, nothing else), or "what share of all Earth's
% water is in the ground?" (abstain — the source gives ground water as 30%
% OF FRESHWATER, and converting bases is arithmetic it does not perform).
%
% It states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries.
%
% THE THIRD COLUMN IS THE POINT. No query can retrieve a share without also
% retrieving its denominator, so "over 96 percent" and "over 68 percent"
% can never be read as comparable: the first is of all Earth's water, the
% second of the 2.5% of it that is fresh. Confusing those two is the
% commonest error made with these figures.
%
% NOTE ON THE ABSTAIN QUERIES: they are written in VARIABLE form. A
% fully-bound query that matches nothing produces NO recall entry at all
% rather than an abstention, so the ground form would silently prove
% nothing.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli water-share.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "water-share.adj"

? water_share(ice_and_glaciers, $S, $B)          % expect share_over_68_percent OF all_freshwater -- the base comes back WITH the share
? water_share(rivers, $S, $B)                    % expect share_0_49_percent OF surface_freshwater
? water_share($P, $S, surface_freshwater)        % expect lakes AND rivers, nothing else (reverse by base)
? water_share($P, $S, all_earths_water)          % expect saline_water AND freshwater only
? water_share(ground, $S, all_earths_water)      % expect abstain -- stated as 30% OF FRESHWATER; converting bases is arithmetic this source never performs
? water_share($P, share_96_percent, $B)          % expect abstain -- the source says "over 96 percent"; the bare exact figure is not a value
? water_share(atmosphere, $S, $B)                % expect abstain -- appears in the page's TABLES, which tag-stripping cannot quote byte-faithfully
